API Endpoints:
POST /auth/register: Register a new user.

POST /auth/login: Login a user and return a JWT token.

GET /users/me: Retrieve user profile (requires authentication).

GET /books: Retrieve all books from the database.

GET /books/:id: Retrieve a single book by ID.

POST /books: Admin-only endpoint to add a new book.

PUT /books/:id: Admin-only endpoint to update a book.

DELETE /books/:id: Admin-only endpoint to delete a book.

POST /reviews: Add a review for a book.

PUT /reviews/:id: Edit an existing review.

DELETE /reviews/:id: Delete a review.

Features:
User Authentication: Secure login/signup system using JWT.

Admin Panel: Admins can manage books, authors, and users.

Books CRUD: Admins can create, read, update, and delete books.

Review System: Users can add/edit/delete reviews for books.

Database Schema
Tables:
Users: Stores user details like email, password hash, and roles (admin, author, user).

Books: Stores book details like title, author, genre, and description.

Reviews: Stores user reviews, including ratings and text.

Genres: Stores book genres.

